{
  "id": "candidate-applied-nonlinear-cruise-pi",
  "name": "Nonlinear Vehicle Cruise with Leaky PI and Hill",
  "category": "transportation",
  "description": "Source1600 kg vehicle, gear4,20 m/s reference,4-degree slope ramp5\u20136s and25 s horizon. Initial state is the computed exact closed-loop equilibrium for fixed20 m/s command, rather than the source find_eqpt routine allowed to adjust that command. Retains author throttle/torque saturation and controller leak. Primary model: \u00c5str\u00f6m and Murray, Feedback Systems, second edition, author BSD 3-Clause Python source pinned dbbc2e1b4233dc148a3dc52c10d08e87881c1f15. Numerical grid is our explicit choice. No empirical calibration or safety-control guarantee. Units not supplied where a coherent physical annotation has not been established.",
  "source": "https://github.com/murrayrm/fbs2e-python/blob/dbbc2e1b4233dc148a3dc52c10d08e87881c1f15/cruise.py",
  "reference": "\u00c5str\u00f6m and Murray, Feedback Systems, second edition; author example code cruise.py, figure-1.11-cruise_robustness.py",
